From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:39:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb+LibWebView+WebContent+WebWorker: Launch ImageDecoder
 on demand

Every WebContent and WebWorker process started with an ImageDecoder of
its own, which costs over 20 MiB even for a page or cross-site frame
that has no images, and kept it for its whole life.

Install the image codec plugin without a client, and have it ask the
Browser for a decoder when it first decodes an image, or decodes again
a frame it discarded to save memory. Once the decoder has had no
decodes in flight and no animations for 15 seconds, drop the client,
which makes the decoder exit; the next image starts a new one. A
decoder that crashes is likewise replaced on the next decode, so the
Browser no longer needs to watch for that, nor to send each process a
decoder.

The plugin keeps the decoder while any animation session is live, as
the Compositor asks the decoder for those sessions' frames over a frame
client of its own. That frame client no longer keeps the decoder
process running: it exits once the client it serves has gone, and the
Compositor's channel goes with it.

TestImageDecoderIsolation and the ImageDecoder crash report test now
decode an image before looking for a decoder, and the isolation test
checks that a crashed decoder is replaced on the next decode, the
synchronous one of a discarded frame included.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
